All three changes applied. Here is a summary of what was done:

**Task J3 -- Visual paragraph chunking in `renderText()` (chat.js)**

File: `C:\Users\User\comfyui-agent\ui\web\js\chat.js`, line 68-72

Added a conditional class `sd-para-long` to any paragraph element where the trimmed text exceeds 200 characters. This gives the CSS layer a hook to apply extra margin or other visual treatment to long paragraphs, improving scanability of agent responses.

```javascript
const p = document.createElement("p");
_appendInlineMarkup(p, trimmed);
if (trimmed.length > 200) {
  p.classList.add("sd-para-long");
}
frag.appendChild(p);
```

**Task J4 -- Aria labels for accessibility (sidebar.js)**

File: `C:\Users\User\comfyui-agent\ui\web\js\sidebar.js`, lines 125 and 138

Two changes in the `buildSidebar()` HTML template:

1. The messages container now has `role="log"`, `aria-live="polite"`, and `aria-label="Chat with Super Duper AI"` -- allowing screen readers to announce new messages as they arrive and identify the chat region.

2. The send button now has `aria-label="Send message"` -- providing a clear accessible name for the button action.

